# Wolverine, Fierce Fighter: "When Wolverine enters, he fights up to one other target creature."
# If Wolverine leaves the battlefield before the trigger resolves, no fight damage is dealt to or by him (CR 701.14b),
# and a Wolverine that has been exiled and returned is a new object (CR 400.7), not "he". So the target, still legal,
# neither deals nor takes any damage.
#
# Displacer Kitten is out from turn 7. On turn 9 Wolverine enters and his trigger targets Bot2's Guerrilla Gorilla; in
# response Bot1 casts Lightning Bolt at Bot2, and Kitten's trigger flickers Wolverine. The returned Wolverine's own
# enters trigger targets nothing. When the first trigger resolves the Gorilla takes no damage and deals none, where a
# fight (wolverine-fights-the-creature-he-targets-as-he-enters) would have killed it and marked 2 on Wolverine.

